<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50465" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμάω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		inf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phot.
				</span></i>
			:—<i>draw up</i>, esp. water from a well, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				8.352a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάδῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orib.
					<u>Eup.</u>
					1.1.2
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be tapped of, yield</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					522b12
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PA</u>
				688b10
			</span></i>. (From 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2f
				</span></i>
			, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Ael.Dion.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				211
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμάω</span> has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ</span> (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθιμάω</span>), 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμονιά, ἱμανήθρη</span>
			, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμαῖος</span> has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
